  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">GEO: Green Future: Renewable Energy Awareness for Georgian Youth</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">GREDA will deliver an engaging climate and renewable energy education programme for students aged 14&#x2013;18 across 10 Georgian regions with strong renewable potential. Working with the Ministry of Education and regional Resource Centres, GREDA will run school-based seminars that combine age-appropriate content, hands-on activities, and mini-quizzes to select regional teams. The programme culminates in a national &#x2018;What? Where? When?&#x2019; style quiz final in Tbilisi, motivating students from the regions to excel and providing strong public visibility.

The project advances UK objectives on climate action, inclusive education and youth empowerment, and UK&#x2013;Georgia cooperation in the green transition. It delivers measurable outcomes (students reached, knowledge gains, regional coverage) within a 5-month window at good value by leveraging GREDA&#x2019;s existing materials and regional networks while ensuring safeguarding for minors.</narrative>
  </description>
